# Coach environment variables
#
# API keys are configured in the app Settings window.
#
# Do not put Soniox, Anthropic, or OpenRouter keys in VITE_* variables:
# Vite exposes them to the frontend bundle.

# ── Build-time (Rust/Cargo, not Vite) ────────────────────────────────────────
# COACH_MODEL_MIRROR — where the CAM++ speaker-diarization model is downloaded
# from on first use. Unset means the app falls back to a third-party GitHub
# release we do not control; if that release is retired, diarization breaks for
# NEW installs only (existing ones keep their cached copy), which makes it a
# quiet failure. Publish our own copy with
# `src-tauri/scripts/fetch-speaker-model.sh` and set this to either the exact
# file URL or a prefix ending in `/`. The SHA-256 is verified on download either
# way, and upstream stays compiled in as a fallback.
# COACH_MODEL_MIRROR=https://cdn.example.com/models/
